{"chunk_id": "8fe1bf0fa83e", "text": "After Kichaka publicly kicks and humiliates Draupadi (disguised as Sairindhri) in King Virata\u2019s court, she fiercely denounces the injustice. She laments that the mighty warriors who are her husbands\u2014the Pandavas, living in disguise\u2014endure the insult in silence. The courtiers sympathize with her beauty and dignity, though King Virata claims ignorance of the dispute. Yudhishthira, bound by their need to remain concealed, restrains Draupadi and urges patience, hinting that her unseen \u201cGandharva husbands\u201d will eventually avenge her. Draupadi bitterly remarks that her husbands are too gentle and vulnerable because their eldest is addicted to dice. Retreating in grief, she resolves to act and secretly seeks Bhima at night. Overcome with anger and humiliation, she wakes him and demands vengeance against Kichaka, setting in motion the plan that will lead to the tyrant\u2019s death.\nAfter Kichaka insults Draupadi, she rebukes the court, is restrained by Yudhishthira, and secretly seeks Bhima at night to avenge the outrage.\nThemes: humiliation and honor, restraint under disguise, appeal for vengeance, courtly injustice, marital loyalty", "vector": [-0.008978422731161118, -0.010586600750684738, 0.006952803116291761, -0.0012839761329814792, 0.006035799626260996, 0.028167065232992172, -0.021693293005228043, -0.008766280487179756, 0.001503817387856543, -0.033532220870256424, 0.01955818012356758, 0.004502898082137108, 0.032601531594991684, 0.0035756295546889305, -0.001823742175474763, 0.016533438116312027, 0.041196729987859726, -0.0012925302144140005, 0.04639764502644539, -0.025799280032515526, 0.002721926663070917, 0.008985266089439392, -0.004848485346883535, 0.017299888655543327, -0.04056714475154877, 0.014699430204927921, 0.015315328724682331, -0.024841217324137688, 4.0097522287396714e-05, -0.006032377947121859, -0.02757854014635086, -0.006148714106529951, 0.006347170099616051, -0.011962106451392174, -0.0428664945